okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Why g:\\ciel-walkie stopped receiving SSE/channel injections again (2026-09-23 morning)."
reported: "User, 2026-09-23: 'g:\\ciel-walkie 에서 다시 sse 주입이벤트를 못받고있는데' then '잠들어있다가 못깨는거같기도하고'"
status: "Diagnosed only; no code changed, the live session and router were not touched."
confirmed:
  instance: "Router 9469-aae7db361c7f (snapshot 7b684132), Claude session 417ef30b-1289-47a5-8921-a4d45eb93f2e, transport session_socket (pipe cc-msg-0b3ee9bc...)."
  current_hold: "Since 08:49 the log repeats every 30 s 'channel_windows_console_deferred cursor=669 reason=active_turn'. runtime-input-status.jsonl holds 670-677 as 'queued' (670-674 then skipped as superseded_channel_notice by the llm-inject path)."
  turn_is_real: "The transcript shows one turn open since 13:44:49Z (the user's typed Request-app request). Its last record is 13:59:50Z: an assistant tool_use running a foreground Bash wait loop (`until gh run view ... = completed; do sleep 20; done`, timeout 600000) with no tool_result yet at 14:04Z. The previous identical loop (13:49:45Z) ran the full 600 s and was moved to the background. active_turn_from_text returns True for a pending tool_use, so the deferral matches the transcript."
  delivery_never_confirmed: "Messages 660 (08:11:31) and 669 (08:37:53) were injected over session_socket and DID reach the model: the transcript has queue-operation enqueue -> dequeue -> a user record 'Another Claude session sent a message:\\n[ciel-runtime external channel message] ... id=669' with isMeta:true and origin {kind: peer}, followed by an assistant end_turn reply (669 answered at 13:38:01Z). The router nevertheless logged channel_windows_console_unseen_failed for both (316 s, 679 s) and the status store recorded 669 as failed/stale_unconfirmed. The whole current router.log has 0 '_confirmed message_id' lines and 8 unseen_failed lines since 2026-09-22 22:41."
  why_unconfirmed: "wake_state_evidence_from_text only accepts user text from is_typed_user_prompt, which returns False for any record where is_non_turn_user_record is True - and that includes isMeta:true. Claude Code persists session-socket (peer) messages as isMeta:true, so the delivered prompt is never admitted as evidence: the state stays 'queued' (enqueue seen) and later 'missing' -> unseen_failed."
  not_enqueued_during_turn: "User correction 2026-09-23: 'the message must reach the queue even while running, but it does not even get queued.' Confirmed: channel_pending_poll.poll_pending_channel_messages (cf41ddb, 2026-07-18) returns before inject_pending whenever services.active() (= polling.active_tool_call() or console.active_turn(), wired in channel_terminal_proxy for 'channel_windows_console'). The session_socket exemption lives inside inject_pending (channel_pending_injection.py:198, `if not requested_session_socket and (active_tool_call or active_turn)`, 60846f9, 2026-09-01), so on the Windows console path it is never reached during a turn. Transcript evidence: the last 15 channel enqueues (07:24Z-14:07Z) all follow a turn_duration/away_summary or a just-typed user record, none mid-tool-call; 670-677 waited through the whole 13:44Z turn and the next enqueue came at 14:07:51Z right after its turn_duration."
inferred:
  - "While a delivered message sits unconfirmed the cursor is held until unseen_retry fires (316-846 s observed), so later messages wait that long even when the session goes idle. Not measured as a separate stall today: 670+ arrived after 669 had already failed, during the real active turn."
  - "Why the unseen timer fired at 679 s rather than ~20 s is not established."
not_done:
  - "No fix, test or deploy - awaiting the user's instruction."
